3. Background-attachment consistency
   - Consider setting desktop attachments uniformly (e.g. `background-attachment: fixed, fixed, fixed;`) instead of mixing attachment values across layers. Mixed values can produce inconsistent behavior if a browser loads only some layers. Alternatively, use `scroll` for all layers to avoid parallax on devices that perform poorly with `fixed`.

4. Repo size & hosting
   - If the generated images are large, consider resizing/adjusting quality or using Git LFS if you intend to keep multiple large assets in the repo.

